WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.000 --> 00:01.000
MkvDrama.net

3
00:04.970 --> 00:07.400
Whoever does Star's missions is someone who likes Star.

4
00:07.400 --> 00:08.630
Listen up, guys.

5
00:08.630 --> 00:10.970
If it's missions or paying 60,000 baht,

6
00:10.970 --> 00:12.600
I'd obviously pick the first, right?

7
00:13.000 --> 00:13.900
Easier than expected.

8
00:14.270 --> 00:15.100
Been together long?

9
00:16.430 --> 00:18.870
Dad! Together? What are you talking about?

10
00:19.230 --> 00:21.100
You could tone down the niceness a bit, Din.

11
00:21.700 --> 00:23.330
But promise me,

12
00:23.330 --> 00:25.230
if it's ever too much, you have to stop.

13
00:25.570 --> 00:26.470
I promise.

14
00:26.470 --> 00:28.070
If it's ever too much, I'll stop.

15
00:28.070 --> 00:29.830
Same for you. You're the captain.

16
00:29.830 --> 00:32.770
If you let your emotions drive every play, how will you lead the team?

17
00:33.800 --> 00:35.030
I'm jealous of you and Chemi.

18
00:35.030 --> 00:38.370
Do you really like me, or is it just the promise from back then?

19
00:38.370 --> 00:40.270
At first I thought we felt the same way.

20
00:40.270 --> 00:41.280
But now I don't know.

21
00:41.280 --> 00:43.030
I have something to sort out first.

22
00:43.030 --> 00:43.770
What is it?

23
00:43.770 --> 00:45.030
It's something about me.

24
00:45.030 --> 00:46.330
You don't have to answer.

25
00:46.330 --> 00:48.930
I think your silence is answer enough.

26
00:48.930 --> 00:50.630
Not being clear is the answer, sweetie.

27
00:50.630 --> 00:52.330
If he wants you in his life,

28
00:52.330 --> 00:54.370
he'll do everything to keep you.

29
00:54.370 --> 00:56.530
If you can't say it, why not write it?

30
00:56.530 --> 00:59.000
When my dad messes up and wants to explain things to my mom,

31
00:59.000 --> 01:00.230
he writes it all down.

32
01:00.230 --> 01:02.170
Damn! Why didn't I think of that?

33
01:02.170 --> 01:04.500
You two are so close. Don't ever break up.

34
01:04.500 --> 01:05.830
I won't ask for much of a dowry.

35
01:05.830 --> 01:08.400
But first, let me win Fuen over.

36
01:09.370 --> 01:10.970
I can always wait for you.

37
01:10.970 --> 01:13.030
But don't get too carried away with me.

38
03:18.829 --> 03:20.400
Chemi. / Yes?

39
03:20.400 --> 03:21.370
Where's Mom?

40
03:21.829 --> 03:23.230
Mom went out.

41
03:23.770 --> 03:26.430
But she made some food for you.

42
03:26.430 --> 03:28.100
Eat if you're hungry.

43
03:29.700 --> 03:32.030
Oh, Aof, this is Chemi, my little brother.

44
03:46.130 --> 03:47.670
If you're still single by then,

45
03:47.670 --> 03:49.400
I'll be your first boyfriend myself.

46
03:50.270 --> 03:52.370
Then promise me, Aof.

47
04:39.270 --> 04:41.200
Oh, Time, you're here?

48
04:41.200 --> 04:41.930
Mm.

49
04:42.430 --> 04:43.970
So, about our activity,

50
04:43.970 --> 04:45.000
how about a workshop?

51
04:46.700 --> 04:50.200
I don't think so. It'll overlap with the booths downstairs.

52
04:50.200 --> 04:53.100
And we've got the whole room.

53
04:53.100 --> 04:55.400
Why don't we do something that fills it?

54
04:56.470 --> 04:58.000
Fills the whole room?

55
04:58.770 --> 04:59.730
A cafe?

56
05:03.100 --> 05:03.930
Board games?

57
05:05.130 --> 05:06.370
Not games either?

58
05:07.300 --> 05:08.230
A haunted house?

59
05:11.600 --> 05:12.900
Then what?

60
05:17.300 --> 05:18.300
I've got it.

61
05:18.590 --> 05:19.300
What?

62
05:19.300 --> 05:21.470
Let's make this room a surprise for everyone.

63
05:21.470 --> 05:22.670
Sure. What is it?

64
05:26.100 --> 05:27.870
Sure. Cool. Let's do it.

65
05:28.730 --> 05:30.100
Yeah, let's.

66
05:34.630 --> 05:36.630
Mm-hmm. Makes sense.

67
05:36.630 --> 05:38.900
See? There are two exits, perfect.

68
06:40.030 --> 06:42.200
Chemi, there's something I want to say.

69
06:42.930 --> 06:44.230
I'm sorry, Chemi,

70
06:45.330 --> 06:47.430
for being so slow with everything.

71
06:49.430 --> 06:52.200
And I'm scared I'll say the wrong thing again.

72
06:53.730 --> 06:54.970
So...

73
07:02.130 --> 07:04.170
Chemi, could you take this, please?

74
07:07.030 --> 07:08.470
I spent all night writing it.

75
07:11.070 --> 07:12.830
I want you to read it.

76
07:23.700 --> 07:24.630
Okay.

77
08:06.300 --> 08:08.770
You and I need to talk.

78
08:24.670 --> 08:27.830
I'm not sure you won't hurt my brother again.

79
08:29.530 --> 08:33.730
I'm sorry. But this time I've really thought about how to change.

80
08:34.870 --> 08:37.799
And this time I'm trying to think before I talk.

81
08:38.299 --> 08:40.000
Trying isn't enough.

82
08:40.770 --> 08:42.429
You have to show me.

83
08:48.270 --> 08:51.200
I don't know what the future holds,

84
08:52.970 --> 08:55.470
but whatever you promised my brother,

85
08:55.470 --> 08:57.130
if you hurt him again,

86
08:58.070 --> 08:59.400
as his brother...

87
09:00.270 --> 09:01.700
how could I face you?

88
09:10.930 --> 09:12.070
Physics.

89
09:12.500 --> 09:14.530
Do I really look that bad to you?

90
09:15.500 --> 09:17.600
You're not a bad guy.

91
09:17.600 --> 09:19.530
You just can't get your priorities straight.

92
09:34.570 --> 09:35.630
Is he picking up?

93
09:36.600 --> 09:39.200
No. I've called ten times already.

94
09:39.500 --> 09:40.870
So where is he?

95
09:41.730 --> 09:45.530
I called him on my way here. He said he was in his room.

96
09:46.670 --> 09:48.430
But he's still not here?

97
09:49.500 --> 09:52.000
Don't tell me he forgot Chemi's birthday.

98
09:52.000 --> 09:55.600
Nah. I bet he's just stuck in traffic.

99
09:55.600 --> 09:57.370
Wait for him a bit.

100
09:59.470 --> 10:00.770
I'm not waiting.

101
10:01.070 --> 10:02.300
Just blow them out.

102
10:04.170 --> 10:06.130
Come on, birthday time!

103
10:06.770 --> 10:13.370
Happy birthday to you, happy birthday to you

104
10:13.370 --> 10:19.970
Happy birthday, happy birthday, happy birthday to you

105
10:20.670 --> 10:22.000
Happy birthday!

106
10:22.000 --> 10:25.870
May you be very happy now that you're 15.

107
10:26.400 --> 10:29.670
And stop annoying me like you have the past 14 years.

108
10:32.130 --> 10:33.670
Yes, bro.

109
10:36.270 --> 10:38.270
Whoa, you call that a birthday wish?

110
10:39.600 --> 10:45.100
I hope you meet only good people and good things.

111
10:46.130 --> 10:48.500
I hope you get everything you wish for.

112
10:49.700 --> 10:51.770
Thank you, Fuen.

113
10:51.770 --> 10:54.670
I don't know what your life plans are,

114
10:54.670 --> 10:58.200
but I hope everything goes the way you want.

115
10:59.230 --> 11:01.000
Thank you, guys.

116
11:01.000 --> 11:04.670
I'll make good use of all your wishes.

117
11:05.030 --> 11:05.830
Amen.

118
11:19.900 --> 11:21.300
Hey, let's cut the cake.

119
11:21.300 --> 11:22.930
Cut the cake! Cut the cake!

120
11:34.230 --> 11:36.130
I know you have your reasons,

121
11:36.570 --> 11:39.830
but you should've told everyone, not left them waiting.

122
11:40.870 --> 11:42.070
I'm sorry.

123
11:43.100 --> 11:45.330
I won't let that happen again.

124
11:45.700 --> 11:47.570
Can't you help me out this time?

125
11:49.230 --> 11:50.600
I don't trust you.

126
11:52.230 --> 11:54.570
You've never given me a reason to.

127
11:58.970 --> 12:01.830
Then why don't we wait for Chemi's answer?

128
12:02.930 --> 12:05.730
If he says no... it's over.

129
12:05.730 --> 12:07.100
No need to fight.

130
12:09.800 --> 12:11.970
So you're helping me now, Fuen?

131
12:13.830 --> 12:15.270
What do you want me to do?

132
12:15.830 --> 12:17.570
Say you want to keep going,

133
12:17.730 --> 12:18.870
but he says no.

134
12:19.330 --> 12:21.100
You want me to force him?

135
12:24.530 --> 12:26.400
But I get where Fuen's coming from.

136
12:26.870 --> 12:29.070
But if Chemi's okay with it,

137
12:29.800 --> 12:31.870
would you be okay too, Physics?

138
12:34.570 --> 12:35.930
I'm his brother.

139
12:36.500 --> 12:38.270
I have a right to worry about him.

140
12:39.400 --> 12:43.100
The only way I'll accept it is if you show me.

141
12:46.200 --> 12:47.100
Otherwise,

142
12:48.800 --> 12:50.700
I'm definitely not changing my mind.

143
13:16.930 --> 13:18.130
Chemi.

144
13:18.870 --> 13:21.630
I'm afraid I'll say the wrong thing again

145
13:21.630 --> 13:24.300
and we'll misunderstand each other even more.

146
13:24.300 --> 13:26.970
So I wrote this for you to read instead.

147
13:31.400 --> 13:33.470
When we first met,

148
13:34.600 --> 13:37.370
I thought you were so bright and cheerful.

149
13:38.200 --> 13:40.970
And I wanted to protect you the way Physics does.

150
13:59.570 --> 14:02.070
Careful, it's dangerous.

151
14:02.600 --> 14:04.470
Thank you, Aof.

152
14:04.900 --> 14:07.500
Because I love it when you smile.

153
14:10.870 --> 14:14.530
I'm sorry I never gave you a clear answer when you asked.

154
14:14.530 --> 14:17.330
But now I want to do everything right.

155
14:18.030 --> 14:20.500
Will you give me another chance?

156
14:20.730 --> 14:25.400
♪ Every day goes by, it never fades ♪

157
14:25.400 --> 14:34.030
♪ The feelings back then, the story back then, I still remember ♪

158
14:34.030 --> 14:44.300
♪ The smile you gave me, that day we sat side by side ♪

159
14:44.300 --> 14:54.570
♪ We once made a promise that we'd have each other ♪

160
14:54.570 --> 15:04.830
♪ That day everything seemed so clear, we laughed all day ♪

161
15:06.130 --> 15:07.870
Whatever, then.

162
15:07.870 --> 15:09.370
Woof, woof, woof.

163
15:10.870 --> 15:12.370
Quit messing with me.

164
15:16.130 --> 15:18.630
It's not that I won't listen to you guys.

165
15:20.970 --> 15:23.300
But I want to try one last time.

166
15:24.730 --> 15:26.670
If I still end up getting hurt,

167
15:30.170 --> 15:32.230
at least I'll be done with it for good.

168
15:34.770 --> 15:39.430
Then next time something's up, you tell us.

169
15:39.430 --> 15:43.130
Or I'll cry if you're hurting and we're not there for you.

170
15:45.530 --> 15:47.230
I'm telling you,

171
15:47.230 --> 15:50.900
if Aof makes you cry even one more time,

172
15:50.900 --> 15:55.170
I swear, I'll kick a ball right in his face.

173
15:55.170 --> 15:56.830
And I'll bite his ear too.

174
16:01.070 --> 16:03.130
I freaking love you guys.

175
16:03.830 --> 16:05.170
Just like that.

176
16:05.930 --> 16:09.800
Looks like the football club's got its own couple.

177
16:09.800 --> 16:10.900
Whoa.

178
16:10.900 --> 16:13.600
Who'd dare boss you around now? / Right.

179
16:13.600 --> 16:15.630
Your boyfriend's the team captain.

180
16:15.630 --> 16:18.970
Easy, guys. I haven't decided yet.

181
16:48.500 --> 16:49.630
What's on your mind?

182
16:49.630 --> 16:50.900
Yeah, what?

183
16:50.900 --> 16:52.370
About Din?

184
16:53.570 --> 16:55.200
Hmm... sure.

185
16:55.200 --> 16:56.930
So? Spill it.

186
16:58.270 --> 16:59.400
Din.

187
16:59.400 --> 17:01.500
Did you take Star home?

188
17:01.930 --> 17:03.230
And what about Rei?

189
17:03.230 --> 17:05.470
Ugh, no idea.

190
17:06.730 --> 17:08.869
I just don't get it.

191
17:09.500 --> 17:11.599
Din wants my LINE ID, right?

192
17:11.599 --> 17:13.500
But why go to so much trouble?

193
17:13.500 --> 17:16.700
I told him he didn't have to go this far.

194
17:19.400 --> 17:21.470
You took him all the way home

195
17:21.470 --> 17:23.800
just to get Star's contact?

196
17:26.130 --> 17:27.329
Because Din likes Star.

197
17:27.329 --> 17:28.400
Correct.

198
17:28.730 --> 17:31.300
Stop it! Yesterday,

199
17:31.300 --> 17:34.900
I told Din not to wait for me after class. I'd go home myself.

200
17:34.900 --> 17:37.900
But he waited till I was done, set on taking me home.

201
17:37.900 --> 17:40.200
Said he'd promised my dad.

202
17:40.770 --> 17:44.070
And when we got home, my dad invited him to dinner.

203
17:44.300 --> 17:45.700
Because Din likes Star.

204
17:45.700 --> 17:46.830
Plus one.

205
17:46.830 --> 17:47.670
Time!

206
17:48.030 --> 17:51.100
But yesterday Dad and Din talked for ages,

207
17:51.100 --> 17:52.630
I could barely get a word in.

208
17:52.900 --> 17:53.970
Right up Dad's alley.

209
17:53.970 --> 17:54.900
Exactly.

210
18:01.700 --> 18:03.530
Let me take a breather.

211
18:06.100 --> 18:07.700
Or maybe...

212
18:08.430 --> 18:10.170
I don't want to think it,

213
18:10.900 --> 18:13.970
but I think you like Star.

214
18:13.970 --> 18:17.430
And say Din does start hitting on you,

215
18:17.430 --> 18:20.100
what would our dear Star do?

216
18:24.330 --> 18:25.670
Stop the nonsense.

217
18:26.230 --> 18:29.870
I promised his dad. Taking him home is normal, right?

218
18:30.900 --> 18:32.470
You definitely like him.

219
18:34.000 --> 18:35.070
Quit stirring.

220
18:35.670 --> 18:36.930
He doesn't like me.

221
18:37.200 --> 18:38.670
Din doesn't like me.

222
18:39.530 --> 18:40.600
The end.

223
18:41.500 --> 18:43.170
Go on, go study.

224
18:43.170 --> 18:44.770
Ugh, what a drag.

225
18:49.400 --> 18:51.200
Talking to you guys gives me a headache.

226
18:51.700 --> 18:54.530
So what's the deal? Huh?

227
18:54.970 --> 18:56.930
Did you talk to Kim?

228
18:56.930 --> 19:00.870
He writes great scripts, even wins contests,

229
19:00.870 --> 19:03.630
but he doesn't open up to people easily.

230
19:03.630 --> 19:07.100
Yeah, I did. He said to meet in the meeting room after class.

231
19:07.700 --> 19:10.600
Good. And watch what you say.

232
19:10.600 --> 19:11.300
Yeah.

233
19:13.070 --> 19:15.400
Does he want our help with anything?

234
19:17.000 --> 19:18.200
He does.

235
19:19.070 --> 19:21.670
Listen carefully.

236
19:22.200 --> 19:25.300
He says the lead has to be you, no one else.

237
19:25.670 --> 19:27.900
The school's Thai dance prodigy.

238
19:27.900 --> 19:28.930
What!

239
19:28.930 --> 19:31.870
What? What do you want me to do?

240
19:31.870 --> 19:33.600
Be in the stage play.

241
19:33.600 --> 19:36.070
Whoa, no way.

242
19:36.070 --> 19:37.830
Ask someone else.

243
19:38.370 --> 19:39.770
Or how about Physics?

244
19:40.400 --> 19:41.700
Huh? Me?

245
19:41.700 --> 19:43.800
Physics can't do it.

246
19:44.270 --> 19:47.970
What would it take for you to do it, Fuen?

247
19:51.200 --> 19:55.630
Okay, if you want me in it, you have to cast someone close to me too.

248
19:56.270 --> 19:59.400
Or I won't do it even if it kills me.

249
19:59.400 --> 20:03.370
It's a khon story, too. A school legend. It's hard.

250
20:03.370 --> 20:05.670
I knew you'd say that.

251
20:05.670 --> 20:06.830
But don't worry.

252
20:06.830 --> 20:08.670
I've got it all planned.

253
20:11.000 --> 20:15.400
My play isn't pure khon. It's contemporary Thai.

254
20:15.400 --> 20:19.070
And besides, your co-star is Din.

255
20:24.800 --> 20:27.730
See you in the main hall after class.

256
20:36.970 --> 20:38.570
Did I just mess up?

257
20:39.200 --> 20:43.300
Why does it feel like he had this all planned?

258
20:45.130 --> 20:47.900
So what role did he give you?

259
20:49.930 --> 20:51.330
Lord Thapfah.

260
20:53.930 --> 20:56.000
Go tell him now. I'll play opposite you.

261
20:56.000 --> 20:57.430
Bro...

262
21:00.800 --> 21:02.270
Um, so...

263
21:02.270 --> 21:04.400
There's something I want to talk about.

264
21:05.500 --> 21:06.300
Mm.

265
21:07.470 --> 21:09.970
But promise you won't get mad.

266
21:12.000 --> 21:12.800
Mm.

267
21:13.670 --> 21:14.530
Promise.

268
21:15.170 --> 21:16.500
Are you telling me or not?

269
21:16.500 --> 21:17.600
I am.

270
21:19.470 --> 21:20.830
It's about Aof...

271
21:20.830 --> 21:21.930
Chemi.

272
21:23.230 --> 21:27.970
Bro, I know I'm making you worry.

273
21:28.800 --> 21:33.800
But I promise if anything happens,

274
21:34.530 --> 21:37.700
I'll put myself first.

275
21:40.400 --> 21:42.870
And if I feel like I'm going to get hurt,

276
21:42.870 --> 21:45.030
I'll get myself out right away.

277
21:49.070 --> 21:58.630
Bro... give me one more chance, please?

278
22:03.970 --> 22:05.430
Okay, okay. Fine.

279
22:07.000 --> 22:08.300
You're not mad?

280
22:08.300 --> 22:10.070
I am. / What?

281
22:10.070 --> 22:12.370
If you don't keep your promise to me.

282
22:13.700 --> 22:15.130
Got it.

283
22:41.700 --> 22:43.530
Be firm about it.

284
22:43.530 --> 22:45.200
No means no.

285
22:49.000 --> 22:51.600
Yeah, trust me.

286
23:07.470 --> 23:09.470
Guys!

287
23:15.370 --> 23:16.830
I...

288
23:17.700 --> 23:18.730
I...

289
23:25.830 --> 23:27.630
What do I have to do?

290
23:40.100 --> 23:42.300
If you don't want to do it, just tell me.

291
23:42.570 --> 23:45.300
I only just found out he wants us to play opposite each other.

292
23:45.630 --> 23:47.070
You can't, Fuen.

293
23:48.270 --> 23:51.030
This role fits you best.

294
23:56.100 --> 23:56.970
Oh, Din.

295
23:56.970 --> 23:58.030
Hey.

296
23:58.630 --> 23:59.730
I'm heading home.

297
23:59.730 --> 24:01.330
Hey, wish me luck.

298
24:02.800 --> 24:04.070
Yeah, yeah. Thanks.

299
24:05.630 --> 24:06.870
These guys are so forgetful.

300
24:06.870 --> 24:07.730
Yeah, I'm off.

301
24:07.730 --> 24:08.630
See ya.

302
24:17.970 --> 24:19.800
Tuck your shirt in, man.

303
24:19.800 --> 24:20.670
Oh, okay.

304
24:32.730 --> 24:35.170
Fuen, just do it.

305
24:35.170 --> 24:36.570
I don't want to rethink this.

306
24:36.970 --> 24:38.630
I saw you present in class once.

307
24:39.270 --> 24:40.730
You bluff like a pro.

308
24:40.730 --> 24:41.930
I don't bluff.

309
24:42.370 --> 24:43.170
True.

310
24:43.600 --> 24:47.170
Even if you forget your lines, you'll still wing it.

311
24:58.870 --> 25:01.300
Don't worry. I'll sort it out with him.

312
25:01.300 --> 25:02.300
Din,

313
25:02.800 --> 25:05.530
I think we should let Fuen decide.

314
25:17.170 --> 25:19.230
Physics, Physics.

315
25:23.400 --> 25:25.930
Give me a minute.

316
25:32.470 --> 25:33.270
Wow.

317
25:34.130 --> 25:35.800
Standing still like a boy band.

318
25:36.370 --> 25:38.070
Want a part?

319
25:44.700 --> 25:46.430
Hey, everyone, back to work.

320
26:06.630 --> 26:08.200
Chemi, listen to me.

321
26:09.600 --> 26:12.030
Let me take care of you again.

322
26:13.000 --> 26:16.470
I promise this time I'll do my best.

323
26:17.300 --> 26:19.830
And I won't be unkind to you anymore.

324
26:23.770 --> 26:24.630
Aof.

325
26:24.630 --> 26:26.600
Don't turn me down yet.

326
26:26.600 --> 26:28.130
Well... / It's not that.

327
26:29.770 --> 26:34.570
I just... wanted to say...

328
26:35.800 --> 26:39.300
what you said just now... was better than what you wrote.

329
26:42.430 --> 26:43.630
And...

330
26:47.370 --> 26:49.600
I'll give you another chance.

331
26:55.900 --> 26:57.300
Yay!

332
26:57.830 --> 26:59.170
Really, Chemi?

333
26:59.670 --> 27:00.770
You mean it, right?

334
27:00.770 --> 27:01.730
There are people around.

335
27:02.230 --> 27:03.730
You're really giving me a chance?

336
27:03.730 --> 27:04.830
Get down. You're heavy.

337
27:07.530 --> 27:11.030
Sorry if I got a little too excited.

338
27:11.930 --> 27:14.430
I thought you'd never give me another chance.

339
27:18.870 --> 27:24.570
♪ Every question in my heart has an answer now ♪

340
27:24.570 --> 27:30.670
♪ No matter how the story goes, in the end my answer is you ♪

341
27:40.030 --> 27:42.270
It's only been one day.

342
27:43.770 --> 27:46.970
I waited four years for you.

343
27:47.600 --> 27:50.360
♪ Because of you, a world that was all noise ♪

344
27:50.360 --> 27:55.020
♪ showed someone who was lost the way to his own heart ♪

345
27:55.020 --> 27:56.300
♪ all I've searched for ♪

346
27:56.300 --> 27:58.170
Thank you, Chemi.

347
27:58.170 --> 28:03.100
♪ Every question in my heart has an answer now ♪

348
28:03.100 --> 28:08.800
♪ No matter how the story goes, in the end my answer is you ♪

349
28:08.800 --> 28:11.300
Take good care of me.

350
28:23.330 --> 28:26.900
Will you tell me now why you don't want me in it?

351
28:29.530 --> 28:31.630
It's written all over your face.

352
28:31.630 --> 28:33.770
Something's definitely up.

353
28:40.830 --> 28:42.930
There's a kiss scene.

354
28:42.930 --> 28:44.500
Didn't you read the script?

355
28:44.500 --> 28:46.430
What! Seriously?

356
28:48.430 --> 28:50.400
Mm.

357
28:50.400 --> 28:55.200
And how could I stand watching you kiss someone else?

358
28:55.200 --> 28:58.370
And it's Din, of all people.

359
29:01.370 --> 29:03.900
I don't feel anything for Din anymore.

360
29:04.530 --> 29:07.430
And Din's already given up on me.

361
29:08.200 --> 29:10.030
Fuen.

362
29:10.670 --> 29:14.270
If you were me,

363
29:15.130 --> 29:16.900
how would you feel?

364
29:17.500 --> 29:18.900
Come on, tell me.

365
29:31.030 --> 29:34.730
Din and I really are just friends now.

366
29:42.900 --> 29:46.030
You want to do it that badly?

367
29:49.070 --> 29:51.370
If I don't do it,

368
29:51.900 --> 29:54.370
won't I look selfish?

369
29:55.400 --> 29:58.300
I admit it. I want to do it.

370
29:59.530 --> 30:04.700
But I'm not sure I can pull it off.

371
30:16.500 --> 30:18.600
Whatever you set your mind to,

372
30:18.600 --> 30:20.870
you always pull it off.

373
30:25.000 --> 30:28.700
Do it. I'm fine.

374
30:36.000 --> 30:37.570
Physics.

375
30:43.530 --> 30:45.200
Really?

376
30:45.200 --> 30:46.530
For real?

377
30:47.430 --> 30:49.800
Yeah, really, it's fine.

378
30:51.900 --> 30:53.930
Really? / Hey.

379
30:54.730 --> 30:56.970
It's fine. Really.

380
31:04.500 --> 31:06.730
Physics.

381
31:10.530 --> 31:12.630
I have an answer for you now.

382
31:13.270 --> 31:14.970
Just hang on a little longer.

383
31:15.730 --> 31:18.670
I want to see the fireworks with you too.

384
31:36.000 --> 31:40.700
So give it your all, okay?

385
31:44.530 --> 31:45.930
Go.

386
32:03.030 --> 32:04.300
Physics!

387
32:04.930 --> 32:06.770
Come here so I can kick you.

388
32:07.670 --> 32:08.470
Hey.

389
32:25.430 --> 32:26.730
Kim,

390
32:28.630 --> 32:31.930
I'm not sure I can do this well,

391
32:33.900 --> 32:35.670
but I'll try.

392
32:37.800 --> 32:40.430
Yes, Lord Thapfah.

393
33:00.300 --> 33:01.470
I'm beat today.

394
33:01.470 --> 33:02.970
Yeah, today was exhausting.

395
33:03.230 --> 33:05.920
Want to grab dessert before tutoring?

396
33:05.920 --> 33:06.630
Sure.

397
33:06.630 --> 33:07.970
Coming? / Let's go.

398
33:08.470 --> 33:09.570
What should we get?

399
33:11.770 --> 33:13.300
Star... it's Rei.

400
33:14.530 --> 33:15.530
Star!

401
33:15.530 --> 33:16.670
Rei.

402
33:17.370 --> 33:19.730
What are you doing here?

403
33:20.070 --> 33:21.970
You've got tutoring, right?

404
33:21.970 --> 33:24.930
I want to talk. Let me take you.

405
33:29.200 --> 33:33.370
Please, Star. I really need your advice.

406
33:33.870 --> 33:35.130
Okay.

407
33:37.730 --> 33:40.600
I'll go on ahead, then.

408
33:41.870 --> 33:42.670
Yeah.

409
33:50.270 --> 33:51.500
What do we do?

410
33:51.500 --> 33:52.830
Ask the group chat for help.

411
33:52.830 --> 33:53.800
Go on.

412
33:56.130 --> 33:57.870
Guys, we've got a problem.

413
33:58.230 --> 33:59.730
Rei took Star away.

414
33:59.730 --> 34:00.980
"WTF, where?" / "You lost him?"

415
34:00.980 --> 34:02.790
"Does Time know?" / "Now what?" / "Send Din!"

416
34:02.790 --> 34:04.400
"Din's at the play." / "Mission! Think!"

417
34:04.400 --> 34:06.770
"Who can go look?" / "I'll send Din. Booboo, Tue, go look."

418
34:12.600 --> 34:16.570
Why do you share this seat with me?

419
34:16.570 --> 34:18.600
It is my duty to guard you,

420
34:18.600 --> 34:20.870
so I must stay as close to you as I can, must I not?

421
34:21.400 --> 34:23.370
Where else would you have me be?

422
34:33.500 --> 34:34.600
Cut.

423
34:35.070 --> 34:38.530
Oh, damn.

424
34:38.770 --> 34:41.600
My heart was racing. I was so tense.

425
34:42.230 --> 34:46.100
Sorry, Din. I flubbed it so many times and wasted your time.

426
34:46.100 --> 34:49.730
It's fine. I'm just grateful you agreed to help.

427
34:50.230 --> 34:52.530
You guys are amazing.

428
34:53.130 --> 34:55.530
Oh, Din, can we talk?

429
34:55.530 --> 34:56.870
Sure.

430
35:08.000 --> 35:09.170
So?

431
35:09.170 --> 35:10.800
How was that?

432
35:12.170 --> 35:15.230
Good. Told you you could do it.

433
35:17.400 --> 35:18.700
Give me your hand.

434
35:18.700 --> 35:20.300
I'm hungry.

435
35:20.970 --> 35:23.430
But no one's home today.

436
35:23.430 --> 35:25.130
Come cook for me.

437
35:27.500 --> 35:28.730
Sure.

438
35:30.700 --> 35:32.870
Uh, guys.

439
35:33.670 --> 35:34.730
Kim,

440
35:35.130 --> 35:36.330
rehearsal's over, right?

441
35:36.330 --> 35:37.200
Yes.

442
35:37.200 --> 35:38.430
I'll head out first.

443
35:38.430 --> 35:39.330
Oh, sure.

444
35:49.670 --> 35:51.370
Where's Din rushing off to?

445
35:51.800 --> 35:53.330
A mission.

446
35:53.830 --> 35:54.770
Oh.

447
35:55.970 --> 35:59.330
Time, dear, I think we need to talk.

448
35:59.730 --> 36:01.770
I've been waiting to talk to you guys too.

449
36:02.600 --> 36:03.970
I want to know too.

450
36:03.970 --> 36:05.230
Sure.

451
36:05.230 --> 36:07.070
The more help, the better.

452
36:08.500 --> 36:09.700
So here's the thing.

453
36:09.970 --> 36:13.200
"Mission 2: Save Star from Rei"

454
36:28.100 --> 36:29.770
Are you hungry, Chemi?

455
36:32.630 --> 36:35.930
A little.

456
36:36.870 --> 36:38.570
What about you, Aof?

457
36:38.570 --> 36:39.900
I'm getting hungry.

458
36:41.270 --> 36:44.200
Want to find something to eat?

459
36:44.730 --> 36:46.830
Let's try this place, Chemi.

460
36:51.600 --> 36:54.070
This place is going viral right now.

461
36:54.070 --> 36:57.030
I've wanted to try it for ages. Let's go.

462
36:57.570 --> 36:58.730
Okay.

463
36:59.500 --> 37:02.030
If you want it, let's go.

464
37:04.730 --> 37:07.300
Welcome to Gentia Cafe!

465
37:10.170 --> 37:11.900
What would you like, Aof?

466
37:13.070 --> 37:14.630
You order first, Chemi.

467
37:15.900 --> 37:20.730
I'll have a Matcha Sommerso, less sweet.

468
37:22.000 --> 37:26.870
And I'll have a Truffle Milk Sommerso, extra, extra sweet.

469
37:28.400 --> 37:30.330
Sweet tooth, huh?

470
37:39.970 --> 37:42.170
You want this one, Chemi?

471
37:47.170 --> 37:51.030
Excuse me, how do I get this promotion?

472
37:51.030 --> 37:54.470
Spend 2,000 baht. You need 1,760 more.

473
37:54.470 --> 37:56.900
Then I'll take anything to make it 2,000.

474
37:56.900 --> 37:58.270
Wow, sure.

475
38:15.370 --> 38:17.470
Oh, thank you.

476
38:22.900 --> 38:24.570
One sec.

477
38:26.530 --> 38:28.230
Smile, Chemi.

478
38:46.600 --> 38:48.670
One each for us to keep.

479
38:49.570 --> 38:51.130
Thank you.

480
38:56.430 --> 38:58.770
Hello, feel free to look around.

481
38:58.770 --> 39:00.570
We have a new collection in.

482
39:13.170 --> 39:14.570
Like it?

483
39:17.070 --> 39:19.000
No, just...

484
39:19.000 --> 39:21.530
it's pretty, and it's the new collection.

485
39:21.870 --> 39:22.970
Thank you.

486
39:22.970 --> 39:24.000
Let's go.

487
39:24.300 --> 39:25.030
Excuse me.

488
39:25.030 --> 39:26.900
Two of these, please.

489
39:27.300 --> 39:28.830
400 baht. / Sure.

490
39:29.300 --> 39:30.030
Here.

491
39:30.030 --> 39:30.970
Thank you. One moment.

492
39:31.330 --> 39:32.170
Sure.

493
39:41.200 --> 39:44.700
Aof, can we take it slow?

494
39:45.130 --> 39:48.300
I don't want you pushing yourself too hard.

495
39:48.300 --> 39:50.000
You'll wear yourself out.

496
39:50.000 --> 39:51.430
I'm not tired.

497
39:51.430 --> 39:53.000
Because I'm not even trying.

498
39:54.570 --> 39:57.470
I told you, this time I'll do my best.

499
40:09.330 --> 40:13.530
For me, this is nothing.

500
40:23.670 --> 40:24.730
Cute, right?

501
40:54.070 --> 40:56.000
What are you looking at, Aof?

502
40:57.370 --> 40:59.170
Oh, nothing.

503
41:00.470 --> 41:02.970
Let's get going. Come on.

504
41:04.200 --> 41:06.030
What do you want to eat, Chemi?

505
41:07.300 --> 41:08.430
Noodles.

506
41:08.430 --> 41:10.270
Noodles? / Yup.

507
41:11.030 --> 41:12.570
That place?

508
41:21.300 --> 41:23.430
You can drop me here, Rei.

509
41:24.330 --> 41:25.870
You don't want me to walk you in?

510
41:26.230 --> 41:28.230
I need to hurry to class.

511
41:28.230 --> 41:31.300
And honestly, if this is all you want to talk about,

512
41:31.300 --> 41:32.900
you can just call me.

513
41:35.070 --> 41:37.000
Am I making you uncomfortable, Star?

514
41:38.370 --> 41:41.000
I know what you're thinking, Rei.

515
41:41.430 --> 41:43.970
But you're really just a big brother to me.

516
41:44.430 --> 41:47.270
I don't think it can be more than that.

517
41:49.230 --> 41:52.400
I get it. Go to class.

518
41:52.600 --> 41:54.330
I'll keep my distance.

519
41:56.070 --> 41:57.930
I'll go to class, then.

520
42:06.830 --> 42:07.930
Si.

521
42:09.930 --> 42:13.130
Hey, Si, did you buy this for me?

522
42:15.100 --> 42:17.370
Huh? I didn't buy it.

523
42:19.200 --> 42:20.270
Huh?

524
42:21.930 --> 42:24.030
Then whose is this?

525
42:24.030 --> 42:26.200
It was already here when I got here.

526
42:26.200 --> 42:28.470
I thought you'd gotten here first, Star.

527
42:39.630 --> 42:41.830
See you, Star. Thanks for the snacks.

528
42:41.830 --> 42:43.830
Bye-bye. Enjoy.

529
42:49.870 --> 42:50.670
Hey.

530
42:54.300 --> 42:56.470
Could someone open the door?

531
42:59.670 --> 43:01.370
Is anyone out there?

532
43:12.900 --> 43:15.430
Oh? / Star.

533
43:22.000 --> 43:23.570
Did something happen in there?

534
43:24.730 --> 43:28.000
Nothing, Din. I was just in a hurry.

535
43:28.600 --> 43:30.200
Everyone's gone home.

536
43:30.200 --> 43:33.170
And the lights around here aren't great, Din.

537
43:36.430 --> 43:37.600
You sure?

538
43:38.870 --> 43:42.530
I'm sure. So, did you come for something?

539
43:43.070 --> 43:45.300
Um, I'm hungry.

540
43:45.700 --> 43:48.500
Didn't you say you'd treat me to a meal?

541
43:48.900 --> 43:50.370
Today?

542
43:50.370 --> 43:51.090
Mm.

543
43:51.430 --> 43:53.130
So I came to find you.

544
43:53.530 --> 43:57.300
Oh. What do you want to eat?

545
43:57.570 --> 44:00.900
Let's walk around. Whichever place has the fewest people.

546
44:04.500 --> 44:07.100
Then let's hurry, Din.

547
44:35.570 --> 44:37.370
Here to help or get in the way?

548
44:38.770 --> 44:43.000
I want to help, but I'm scared I'll mess it up.

549
44:53.100 --> 44:56.070
First, pull the leaves off like this.

550
44:59.100 --> 45:00.530
And when you chop them,

551
45:02.470 --> 45:05.830
not too small, or they'll go mushy when boiled.

552
45:10.500 --> 45:11.800
Trust me.

553
45:13.600 --> 45:14.870
Every time you say that,

554
45:15.870 --> 45:17.700
I get nervous.

555
45:17.700 --> 45:19.230
Last time,

556
45:19.230 --> 45:20.930
you climbed through Star's window.

557
45:21.130 --> 45:22.230
This time,

558
45:23.130 --> 45:26.130
are you going to blow up cabbage in your kitchen?

559
45:27.200 --> 45:29.270
There's something I want to know.

560
45:32.430 --> 45:35.630
You never liked anyone before hitting on me?

561
45:54.000 --> 45:57.630
If I said never, would you believe me?

562
46:08.770 --> 46:12.930
I would, because you've never lied to me.

563
46:16.600 --> 46:18.300
Let's keep going.

564
46:24.730 --> 46:26.000
Want to try?

565
46:26.300 --> 46:28.070
You can eat this?

566
46:28.670 --> 46:30.330
Not yet.

567
46:30.330 --> 46:31.970
Or you can eat it raw.

568
46:31.970 --> 46:33.330
It's usually boiled first.

569
46:33.330 --> 46:34.570
Here, keep chopping.

570
46:55.400 --> 46:56.530
Star.

571
47:05.630 --> 47:10.500
Do you know why I came today?

572
47:13.070 --> 47:15.030
For a mission, probably.

573
47:17.470 --> 47:19.570
I'd be lying if I said it wasn't.

574
47:20.370 --> 47:22.700
Because Time really did give me a mission.

575
47:23.070 --> 47:26.230
I think you should stop doing the missions.

576
47:27.470 --> 47:30.770
If you want my contact, I'll give it to you right now.

577
47:30.770 --> 47:31.800
Why?

578
47:32.470 --> 47:34.630
Are you upset with me about something?

579
47:35.970 --> 47:40.570
No, I just don't want you doing these missions anymore.

580
47:43.370 --> 47:45.370
Can I know why?

581
47:46.530 --> 47:49.700
If it makes sense, I'll stop.

582
47:51.200 --> 47:52.770
I have feelings for you.

583
47:55.930 --> 47:57.430
You might not even realize it,

584
47:57.430 --> 48:02.230
but your kindness makes me get my hopes up.

585
48:02.870 --> 48:07.200
And I don't trust myself if you stay this close to me.

586
48:08.530 --> 48:10.500
Since when?

587
48:15.470 --> 48:17.700
All the time.

588
48:22.770 --> 48:25.370
When you peeled shrimp for me.

589
48:34.630 --> 48:37.070
When you saved me from drowning.

590
48:50.700 --> 48:53.200
When you took care of me.

591
48:57.000 --> 48:59.570
And right now, too.

592
49:07.470 --> 49:11.270
At first I didn't even know how I felt.

593
49:12.200 --> 49:16.570
When my friends said I was acting weird, I didn't think much of it.

594
49:19.730 --> 49:22.070
Until you told me straight,

595
49:23.130 --> 49:27.830
then I realized... why I'm here.

596
49:34.000 --> 49:35.070
Star.

597
49:39.000 --> 49:41.630
I have feelings for you too.

598
49:56.130 --> 49:58.630
I'm happy when I do nice things for you.

599
50:02.300 --> 50:05.930
So let me keep doing the missions.

600
50:08.100 --> 50:11.600
And can I add one more rule between us?

601
50:14.170 --> 50:15.630
What is it?

602
50:16.770 --> 50:19.800
If something I do makes you happy,

603
50:20.600 --> 50:24.370
add some letters for me, based on how you feel.

604
50:26.170 --> 50:27.470
It may not be like...

605
50:28.370 --> 50:30.330
collecting stars in kindergarten,

606
50:31.730 --> 50:33.730
but if they're stars from Star,

607
50:34.630 --> 50:36.570
I'd be really proud.

608
50:45.830 --> 50:47.070
Sure.

609
50:48.200 --> 50:50.670
So how many letters do I have now?

610
51:43.470 --> 51:45.930
Keep up the quality, okay?

611
51:45.930 --> 51:47.330
Yes.

612
51:48.200 --> 51:50.000
There's a long way to go,

613
51:50.930 --> 51:53.100
but I'll help you,

614
51:53.100 --> 51:54.800
and stay by your side.

615
51:57.400 --> 51:59.700
Get home safe.

616
52:07.630 --> 52:09.200
Dad!

617
52:09.200 --> 52:13.330
How long are you going to stand there? The mosquitoes are eating me alive.

618
52:14.800 --> 52:18.300
If you're going to flirt, do it inside.

619
52:18.300 --> 52:19.870
Dad!

620
52:21.100 --> 52:23.070
Hello, sir.

621
52:24.200 --> 52:25.470
Wait inside.

622
52:25.470 --> 52:26.370
Okay.

623
52:53.170 --> 52:54.770
What are you doing?

624
52:57.070 --> 52:58.530
Nice bracelet.

625
52:59.070 --> 52:59.900
Is it?

626
52:59.900 --> 53:01.430
Someone bought it for me.

627
53:03.300 --> 53:04.800
Not that I'm bragging.

628
53:12.900 --> 53:14.870
Thanks for walking me home.

629
53:15.370 --> 53:18.300
Let me know when you get home.

630
53:18.300 --> 53:19.500
Shure fing~

631
53:20.700 --> 53:21.830
Sure thing.

632
53:21.830 --> 53:23.870
Mm, that's it. Correct.

633
53:24.900 --> 53:26.700
You're funny these days.

634
53:27.500 --> 53:30.400
Mm, I'm going.

635
53:32.570 --> 53:33.700
Bye-bye.

636
53:33.700 --> 53:34.830
Bye.

637
53:37.200 --> 53:38.770
Chemi,

638
53:39.900 --> 53:43.200
bad dreams bring ghosts, sweet dreams bring me.

639
53:47.470 --> 53:49.400
Get home safe. It's late.

640
54:14.830 --> 54:15.970
Hello, Mii.

641
54:15.970 --> 54:17.200
What's up, Aof?

642
54:18.970 --> 54:20.700
Come out and see me.

643
54:21.270 --> 54:23.430
There's something I need to talk to you about.

644
54:32.600 --> 54:33.970
"You're scared of being let down."

645
54:33.970 --> 54:35.700
"Deep down, you trust Aof with him." (Fuen)

646
54:35.700 --> 54:37.700
"I thought that once, and got let down." (Physics)

647
54:37.700 --> 54:42.100
"Don't worry, there's a long way to go, but I'll help you and stay by your side." (Star)

648
54:42.100 --> 54:43.630
"Thanks, Physics. Don't worry."

649
54:43.630 --> 54:45.130
"I'll choose what's best for me."

650
54:45.130 --> 54:47.270
"If I get hurt, I'll get over it. Trust me." (Chemi)

651
54:47.570 --> 54:48.830
If Fuen and Din agree,

652
54:48.830 --> 54:51.700
as actors, they should give it their all.

653
54:52.770 --> 54:53.970
Din.

654
54:56.630 --> 54:58.970
I know you take good care of yourself, Time,

655
54:58.970 --> 55:00.800
but let me take even better care of you.

656
55:00.800 --> 55:03.000
You don't have to believe my words, Chemi.

657
55:03.000 --> 55:04.730
Just watch what I do.

658
55:05.930 --> 55:09.700
Didn't you tell me to trust your actions?

659
55:09.700 --> 55:13.070
If I don't lie to you, you'll leave me, right?

660
55:16.000 --> 55:18.200
Then just leave me.

661
55:18.200 --> 55:19.200
MkvDrama.net
